  "development_findings": [
    "Strict-clock fixture used an increment just before a floating-point scheduler deadline; after testing the exact .5-second boundary it now advances .002 rather than .001. Production comparisons are unchanged.",
    "Inspector initially treated ObjectId as a scalar; the actual slot and generation are now displayed.",
    "Existing around/escape tests expected unavailable SearchSmellTarget; they now require its original guarded decision, without inventing a cursor.",
    "Sanitizer movement runs timed out at 60s both concurrently and serially. Unchanged direct execution completed in 58.52s; instrumented CTest deadline alone now provides 120s headroom, with all three intro/reload cycles and assertions retained. All failure and final retry logs are kept."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Normal source smell perception clears the target and does not seed the cursor; registered NPC smell ranges remain zero. No invented autonomous acquisition.",
    "Route-body tests explicitly seed a cursor and use real dead-attacker perception; positive visibility uses a diagnostic-only ray-hit hint.",
    "Private trail movement and GPU regressions are not a complete authored encounter or retail parity proof.",
    "Spectator storage is a guard only; full AI/world saves, multiplayer and remaining M2 required services stay open.",
    "No native macOS run; no dependency/shader/reference/commercial asset changes."
  ],
